  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"5.50.0\"\n  name: maxima\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://sourceforge.net/projects/maxima/files/Maxima-source/${{ version }}-source/${{ name }}-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 0bc4b5e11fe153ef20b24a3a816b668ece5378cc738fa24ca426b62fd6d8fc37\n  patches:\n    # Patches from https://git.sagemath.org/sage.git/tree/build/pkgs/maxima/patches\n    # Fixes a test failure that can occur when the install tree has been\n    # relocated; see https://trac.sagemath.org/ticket/11348\n    - patches/infodir.patch\n    # Fixes a bug in matrix inversion that affects Sage; see\n    # https://sourceforge.net/p/maxima/bugs/2596/\n    - patches/matrixexp.patch\n    # Disables a few tests that currently do not pass, see #14\n    - patches/osx_tests.patch\n    # Disable test that fails with ecl 16.1.2 in some setups\n    - patches/rtest8.patch\n    # Disable tests that started fails in 5.42.2\n    - patches/disable_5_42_2_tests.diff\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: win\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - gnuconfig\n    - libtool\n    - make\n    - texinfo\n    - if: build_platform != target_platform\n      then: ecl\n  host:\n    - ecl\n    # ecl no longer run-exports libatomic_ops (its run_export is ignored in the\n    # ecl feedstock), but its headers are still needed when ecl compiles\n    # maxima's C sources.\n    - libatomic_ops\n    - readline\n    - gmp\n  run:\n    - readline\n    - ${{ pin_compatible('ecl', upper_bound='x.x.x') }}\n    - gmp\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    by_name:\n      - libatomic_ops\n  run_constraints:\n    - sagelib >=10.1\n\ntests:\n  - files:\n      recipe:\n        - run-from-ecl.lisp\n    script:\n      - maxima --version\n      - ecl -shell run-from-ecl.lisp\n\nabout:\n  license: GPL-2.0-or-later\n  license_file: COPYING\n  summary: Maxima is a system for the manipulation of symbolic and numerical expressions.\n  homepage: http://maxima.sourceforge.net/\n  repository: https://sourceforge.net/p/maxima/code/ci/master/tree/\n  documentation: http://maxima.sourceforge.net/documentation.html\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - embray\n    - isuruf\n    - saraedum\n",
